  "id": "hering-illusion",
  "term": "Hering illusion",
  "definition": "The Hering illusion is a visual illusion in which straight lines are seen as bowed. In the supplied source, this effect is produced by an optic-flow background, suggesting the visual system can warp perceived space in the context of motion.",
